        .section-head
          p.eyebrow Learn
          h2 Level Up Your OGC Knowledge
        .grid.grid-2
          .card
            .icon-badge
              svg(viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round")
                path(d="M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z")
                path(d="M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z")
            h3(style="font-size:22px;") OGC API Workshop
            p(style="font-size:15.5px;") This workshop provides a combination of concepts, presentations, and exercises on OGC APIs in support of discovery, access, visualization, and processing — in support of FAIR data principles.
            a.learn(href="https://ogcapi-workshop.ogc.org/") Visit workshop →
          .card
            .icon-badge
              svg(viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round")
                circle(cx="12" cy="8" r="7")
                path(d="M8.21 13.89 7 23l5-3 5 3-1.21-9.12")
            h3(style="font-size:22px;") Location Innovation Academy
            p(style="font-size:15.5px;") This learning platform offers different courses, mostly focused on Spatial Data Infrastructures.
            a.learn(href="https://academy.ogc.org/") Visit academy →

    // MORE RESOURCES
    section.alt
      .wrap
        .section-head
          p.eyebrow More Resources
          h2 You May Also Want to Check
        .grid.grid-3
          .card
            .icon-badge
              svg(viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round")
                path(d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20")
                path(d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z")
            h3 Definitions Server
            p A web-accessible source of information about things ("Concepts") the OGC defines or that communities ask the OGC to host, such as technical terms from application schemas.
            a.learn(href="https://defs.opengis.net/vocprez/") Explore →
          .card
            .icon-badge
              svg(viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round")
                path(d="M21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 0 0 3 8v8a2 2 0 0 0 1 1.73l7 4a2 2 0 0 0 2 0l7-4A2 2 0 0 0 21 16z")
                polyline(points="3.27 6.96 12 12.01 20.73 6.96")
                line(x1="12" y1="22.08" x2="12" y2="12")
            h3 Location Building Blocks
            p Maybe you don't need a complete OGC API, or you need to mix multiple OGC APIs. OGC APIs are developed in discrete building blocks you can mix &amp; match to spatially enable your existing APIs.
            a.learn(href="https://blocks.ogc.org/") Explore →
          .card
            .icon-badge
              svg(viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round")
                path(d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14")
                polyline(points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01")
            h3 Compliance &amp; Certification
            p The OGC Compliance program provides tools to test your implementation and confirm it's compliant to the Standard. Take your application further by applying for a compliance certification.
            a.learn(href="https://www.ogc.org/how-our-compliance-program-works/") Explore →

    // COMMUNITY
    section#community
